# {{lb|en|heraldry}} The lowest third of a [[shield]] (or [[field]]), or an ordinary occupying this space, the [[champagne]]. {{q|Compare {{m|en|terrace}}.}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|1956|month=July|Col. H. C. B. Rogers|Railway Heraldry|w:Railway Magazine||479|The shield was silver, charged with a red cross voided (that is, with the centre cut out and only the edges left), between in chief (that is, above the horizontal limb of the cross) two black dragon's wings, and in '''base''' two red daggers, and in the centre of the cross a black winged helmet; on a red chief (a broad band across the top of the shield), a silver pale (a broad vertical band), and thereon eight black arrows crossed X-wise, four and four, and encircled with a black band, between on the dexter three bendlets (narrow bands slanting from dexter chief to sinister '''base''') enhanced (that is, raised above the centre), and on the sinister a ''fleur-de-lis'', all of gold.}}
