#* {{RQ:Dickens Bleak House|text=... the legion of '''bills''' in the suit have been transformed into mere bills of mortality ...|1}}
# {{senseid|en|banknote}}{{lb|en|US|Canada}} A piece of paper [[money]]; a [[banknote]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1830|author=Anon|title=The Galaxy of Wit: Or, Laughing Philosopher, Being a Collection of Choice Anecdotes, Many of Which Originated in or about "The Literary Emporium"|passage=He gave the change for a three dollar '''bill'''. Upon examination, the '''bill''' proved to be counterfeit.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1935|year_published=19 March 2014|title=Cabins in the Laurel|page=231|isbn= 9781469620770|publisher=University of North Carolina Press|url=https://www.google.co.nz/books/edition/Cabins_in_the_Laurel/4WSVAwAAQBAJ|passage={{...}}So I wropped 'em up in a five dollar '''bill''' and tied 'em up and sent 'em, and they ain't back yet.”}}
