# {{lb|en|UK|{{w|Eton College}}}} A [[list]] of [[pupil]]s to be [[discipline]]d for [[break]]ing [[school]] [[rule]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1875|author=Sir H. C. Maxwell Lyte|title=A History of Eton College, 1440-1875|page=373
|passage=One of the best stories of the period describes the misadventure of a batch of candidates for confirmation whose names were by accident sent up to the Head-Master on a piece of paper identical in size and shape with the "'''bill'''" used by the Masters for the purpose of reporting delinquents. Keate, we are told, insisted on flogging all the boys mentioned in the document {{...}}}}

