===Etymology 2===
{{etymid|en|beak-themed}}
From {{inh|en|enm|bill}}, {{m|enm|bil}}, {{m|enm|bille}}, {{m|enm|bile}}, from {{inh|en|ang|bile|t=beak (of a bird); trunk (of an elephant)}}, of unknown origin. Perhaps from a special use of {{cog|ang|bil}}, {{m|ang|bill|t=hook; sword}} (see below).

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q31528}} {{lb|en|zootomy}} The [[beak]] of a [[bird]], especially when [[small]] or [[flattish]]; sometimes also used with reference to a [[platypus]], [[turtle]], or other [[animal]].
#: {{syn|en|beak<id:Q31528>|neb<id:Q31528>|nib<id:Q31528>|pecker<id:Q31528>}}
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Midsummer|III|I|line=125|text=The woosel cock so black of hue, With orange-tawny '''bill''', The throstle with his note so true, The wren with little quill{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-av|en|title=Fibber McGee and Molly|date=November 3, 1942|episode=Duck Hunting|speaker=Mayor LaTrivia|passage="Army planes." Quack-quack-quack-quack-quack. Who was the one in front with the yellow '''bill'''? Jimmy Doolittle?}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=w:Olivia Judson| title=The hemiparasite season [print version: Under the hemiparasite, ''International New York Times'', 24–25 December 2014, page&nbsp;7]| url=http://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/24/opinion/the-hemiparasite-season.html| archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20141223181330/https://www.nytimes.com/2014/12/24/opinion/the-hemiparasite-season.html| archivedate=23 December 2014| newspaper=w:The New York Times| date=23 December 2014| passage={{...}} The flesh [of the [[mistletoe]] berry] is sticky, and forms strings and ribbons between my thumb and forefinger. For the mistletoe, this viscous goop&nbsp;– and by the way, viscous comes to English from {{l|la|viscum}}&nbsp;– is crucial. The stickiness means that, after eating the berries, birds often regurgitate the seeds and then wipe their '''bills''' on twigs&nbsp;– leading to the seeds' getting glued to the tree, where they can germinate and begin the cycle anew.}}
# {{senseid|en|beaklike projection, especially a promontory}} A [[beaklike]] [[projection]], especially a [[promontory]].
#: {{ux|en|There is a lighthouse on Portland '''Bill'''.}}
# {{senseid|en|Q1639232}} Of a [[cap#Noun|cap]] or [[hat]]: the [[brim#Noun|brim]] or [[peak#Noun|peak]], serving as a [[shade#Noun|shade]] to keep [[sun#Noun|sun]] off the [[face#Noun|face]] and out of the [[eye#Noun|eyes]].
#: {{syn|en|brim<id:Q1639232>|hatbrim<id:Q1639232>}}

