===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[fasten]] a [[#Noun|belt]] on; to [[encircle]] with a belt.
#: {{ux|en|Edgar '''belted''' himself in and turned the car's ignition.}}
#: {{ux|en|The rotund man had difficulty '''belting''' his pants, and generally wore suspenders to avoid the issue.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To encircle; to surround.
#: {{ux|en|The small town was '''belted''' by cornfields in all directions.}}
#* {{RQ:Melville Moby-Dick|[[s:Moby-Dick (1851) US edition/Chapter 1|chapter 1]]|passage=There now is your insular city of the Manhattoes, '''belted''' round by wharves as Indian isles by coral reefs—commerce surrounds it with her surf. Right and left, the streets take you waterward.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[invest]] (a person) with a [[#Noun|belt]] as part of a [[formal]] [[ceremony]] such as [[knighthood]].
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[hit]] with a [[#Noun|belt]].
#: {{ux|en|The child was misbehaving so he was '''belted''' as punishment.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|colloquial}} To [[hit]] [[someone]] or [[something]], especially [[forcefully]]; to [[bash]].
#: {{ux|en|The angry player '''belted''' the official across the face, and as a result was ejected from the game.}}
#* {{quote-song|en|title=w:Three Lions|artist=w:David Baddiel; w:Frank Skinner|year=1996|passage={{w|Bobby Charlton|Bobby}} '''belting''' the ball}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|baseball}} To hit a [[pitch]]ed ball a long distance, usually for a [[home run]].
#: {{ux|en|He '''belted''' that pitch over the grandstand.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive|informal|normally [[belt out]]}} To [[scream]] or [[sing]] in a [[loud]], [[strong]] [[manner]].
#: {{ux|en|He '''belted''' out the national anthem.|footer=(Perhaps a derivative or cognate of {{cog|en|bellow}}, {{cog|fy|balte|t=to howl, shriek}}.)}}
#* {{quote-web|en|url=https://www.bustle.com/p/vanessa-hudgens-cant-stop-crying-about-celine-dion-at-the-2017-billboard-music-awards-honestly-same-video-59371|title=Celine Dion Is Making Everyone Cry|author=Mallory Carra|date=2017-05-22|accessdate=2022-01-01|work=Bustle|publisher=BDG Media|passage=Céline Dion '''belted''' her iconic song "My Heart Will Go On" in a show-stopping performance at the 2017 Billboard Music Awards on May 21. The legendary singer gave the throwback performance in honor of the 20th anniversary of the hit song from the ''Titanic'' soundtrack.}}
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[drink]] quickly, often in [[gulp]]s.
#: {{ux|en|He '''belted''' down a shot of whisky.}}
# {{lb|en|intransitive}} To [[move]], [[run]], [[drive]], etc., very [[fast]].
#: {{ux|en|He was really '''belting''' along.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1983|author={{w|Bill Oddie}}|title=Gone Birding|publisher=Methuen|location=London|page=138|passage=I had to be pretty quick once I'd pulled the string and '''belt''' down the garden before the tiny tits escaped.}}

