===Etymology 1===
{{etymon|en|id=fruit|:inh|enm:berie|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|berie}}, from {{inh|en|ang|berġe}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*baʀi}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*bazją}}.<ref>Marlies Philippa et al., eds., ''Etymologisch Woordenboek van het Nederlands'', A-Z, s.v. “bes” (Amsterdam UP, 3 Dec. 2009) [http://www.etymologie.nl].</ref>

Cognate with {{cog|stq|Bäie}}, {{cog|vls|beier}}, {{cog|de|Beere}}, {{cog|is|ber}}, {{cog|da|bær}}.

The slang sense "police car" may come from the lights on the vehicles' roofs.<ref>{{R:GDoS|pos=n|sense=1|id=hm2zbiy}}</ref>

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# A small [[succulent]] [[fruit]], of any one of many varieties.
# {{lb|en|botany}} A soft fruit which [[develop]]s from a single [[ovary]] and contains [[seed]]s not encased in [[pit]]s.
# A [[coffee bean]].
# One of the [[ovum|ova]] or [[egg]]s of a [[fish]] or [[crustacean]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1877| title=Parliamentary Papers - Volume 24 |author=Great Britain. Parliament. House of Commons | page=7| passage=The crabs carry their '''berries''' for six months.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1913| title=Journals and Printed Papers of the Parliament of Tasmania |author=| page=94| passage=That is the only restriction existing: not even small fish or fish in '''berry''', and there are no restrictions on soft-shelled fish.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1914| title=Minutes and Ordinances - Volume 5 |author=Cape of Good Hope (South Africa). Provincial Council | page=3| passage=These crawfish are speared by the Kafirs, who bring them in to the village for sale, and who catch anything and everything either female fish in '''berry''', or male fish in soft shell. }}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1960| title=Animal and Man in Bible Lands: Supplement |author=Friedrich Simon Bodenheimer | page=86| passage=The corals have the shape of a shrub and are green. Their '''berries''' are snow-white under water and soft. As soon as you take them out of the water, they grow hard and red.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1965| title=Fishery Bulletin of the Fish and Wildlife Service - Volume 65 |author=| page=55| passage=McCormick (1934) stated that eggs in various stages of development were found in females at the same time that they were in '''berry''', which indicates a long egg-laying season.}}
# {{lb|en|slang|US|African American}} A [[police car]].
#* {{quote-song|en|year=1992|author=w:Ice Cube|title=w:It Was a Good Day|album={{w|The Predator (album)|The Predator}}|text=Today was like one of those fly dreams<br>Didn't even see a '''berry''' flashin' those high beams}}
# {{lb|en|US|slang|dated}} A [[dollar]].
#* {{quote-text|en|year=1921|title=Collier's|volume=67|page=365
|passage=Four rounds and Enright still on his feet and a hundred and fifty thousand '''berries''' gone if he stays two more!}}

=====Usage notes=====
* Many fruits commonly regarded as berries, such as [[strawberry|strawberries]] and [[raspberry|raspberries]], are not berries in the botanical sense, while many fruits which are berries in the botanical sense are not regarded as berries in common parlance, such as bananas and pumpkins.

