===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|en|enm|barken}}, {{m|enm|berken}}, {{m|enm|borken}}, from {{inh|en|ang|beorcan|t=to bark}}, from the {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*berkan|t=to bark}}, from {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰerg-|t=to make a noise, growl, bark}}, from {{m|ine-pro|*bʰer-|t=to drone, hum, buzz}}. 

Cognate with {{cog|is|berkja|t=to bark, bluster}}, {{cog|is|barki|t=throat, windpipe}}, dialectal {{cog|lt|burgeti|burgė́ti|t=to growl, grumble, grouch, quarrel}}, {{cog|sh|brbljati|t=to murmur}}. For the noun, compare {{cog|ang|beorc}}, {{m|ang|bearce|t=barking}}.

