# {{senseid|en|Q31528}} {{lb|en|anatomy}}
## A [[rigid]] [[structure]] [[projecting]] from the front of a [[bird]]'s [[face]], used for [[peck]]ing, [[groom]]ing, [[forage|foraging]], [[carry|carrying]] items, [[eat]]ing [[food]], etc.
##: {{syn|en|bill<id:Q31528>|neb<id:Q31528>|nib<id:Q31528>|pecker<id:Q31528>}}
## A similar pointed structure forming the [[nose]] and [[mouth]] of various animals, such as [[turtle]]s, [[platypus]]es, [[whale]]s, ''etc.''
## The long projecting sucking mouth of some [[insect]]s and other [[invertebrate]]s, as in the {{taxfmt|Hemiptera|order}}.
## The upper or projecting part of the shell, near the hinge of a [[bivalve]].
## The [[prolongation]] of certain [[univalve]] shells containing the [[canal]].
## {{lb|en|botany}} Any process somewhat like the beak of a bird, terminating the fruit or other parts of a plant.
# {{lb|en|by extension}}
## Anything projecting or ending in a point like a beak, such as a [[promontory]] of land.
##* {{RQ:Carew Survey of Cornwall
|passage=At the townes end, Cuddenbeak, an ancient house of the Bishops, from a well aduanced Promontory, which intituled it '''Beak'''}}
## {{lb|en|architecture}} A continuous slight projection ending in an [[arris]] or narrow [[fillet]]; that part of a [[drip]] from which the water is thrown off.
## {{lb|en|farriery}} A [[toe clip]].
## {{senseid|en|structural member attached to stem of ship}} {{lb|en|nautical}} That part of a ship, before the [[forecastle]], which is fastened to the [[stem]], and supported by the main [[knee]].
##: {{hol|en|bow<id:Q301897>|stem<id:Q301897>|forestem<id:Q301897>|prow<id:Q301897>|prore<id:Q301897>|<|ship<id:Q11446>|<|vessel<id:Q16391167>}}
## {{senseid|en|battering ram portion of ship_s timber}} {{lb|en|nautical}} A [[beam]], [[shod]] or [[arm#Verb|armed]] at the end with a [[metal]] [[head]] or [[point]], and [[project]]ing from the [[prow]] of an [[ancient]] [[galley]], used as a [[ram]] to [[pierce]] the [[vessel]] of an [[enemy]].
##: {{syn|en|beakhead#Noun}}
##: {{hol|en|bow<id:Q301897>|stem<id:Q301897>|forestem<id:Q301897>|prow<id:Q301897>|prore<id:Q301897>|<|ship<id:Q11446>|<|vessel<id:Q16391167>}}
## {{lb|en|entomology}} Any of various [[nymphalid]] butterflies of the genus {{taxlink|Libythea|genus}}, notable for the beak-like elongation on their heads.
# {{lb|en|slang}}
## A person's [[nose#Noun|nose]], especially one that is large and [[pointed#Adjective|pointed]].
##: {{syn|en|honker|schnozzle}}
##* {{RQ:Doyle Land of Mist|chapter=9|page=186|passage="You mind your own business, curse you!" growled Silas. "I've told you before now not to push that long, sheeny '''beak''' of yours into my affairs. If you was a man I'd know better how to speak to you."}}
