===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|belwen}}, from {{inh|en|ang|belgan}}, {{m|ang|bylgan||to become angry, to swell with rage}}, ultimately from the {{der|en|ine-pro|*bʰel-||to sound, roar}}, whence also {{m|ang|belg||leather bag}}, {{m|ang|bellan||to roar}}, {{m|ang|blāwan||to blow}}. Cognate with {{cog|de|bellen||to bark}}, {{cog|ru|бле́ять||baa, bleat}}.

Compare {{m|en|billow||wave}}, of the same root, also {{m|en|bulge}}, with related etymology to swelling. Potentially related to {{m|en|bawl}}, {{cog|sv|böl||bawl}}.

