#*: Then was the banquetting chamber in the tilt yard at Greenewich, to the which place these strangers were conducted by the noblest personages in the court, where they did both sup and '''banquet'''.
# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[treat]] with a banquet or [[sumptuous]] [[entertainment]] of food; to feast.
#* {{RQ:Shakespeare Taming of the Shrew|act=I|scene=i|passage=Not possible; for who shall bear your part / And be in Padua here Vincentio's son; / Keep house and ply his book, welcome his friends, / Visit his countrymen, and '''banquet''' them?}}
#* '''1800''', {{w|Frederick Schiller}}, ''The Piccolomini, or the First Part of [[w:Wallenstein (trilogy of plays)|Wallenstein]]'', translated by {{w|Samuel Taylor Coleridge}}, London: Longman & Rees, Act I, scene i, p. 2,<sup>[https://archive.org/details/piccolominiadra00colegoog]</sup>
#*: Just in time to '''banquet'''
